    "Item 5 of the rule is report-only. The two runs are NOT identical (differences below). Three runs of the cache backend with the same seed also differ from each other (the run-to-run variation, block run_to_run_variation, n = 3) by amounts of the same size: largest per-round spread 0.0040 validation loss, 0.0034 test loss, 0.141 validation AUC and 0.098 test AUC, against cache-versus-png maxima of 0.0029, 0.0043, 0.022 and 0.024 (only the test-loss maximum is slightly larger). No systematic difference is shown and three runs cannot exclude a small one. The mechanism (non-deterministic GPU kernels) is a hypothesis and was not tested. On the CPU the two backends agree to 1e-5 in the CI end-to-end test.",
    "The AUC values include thin classes only through val/test macro 'excl_thin'; classes with 1 to 7 positives swing the plain macro AUC by several hundredths between any two runs.",
